WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.788
Sandboxed models can

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.319
talk to each

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:03.298
other through shared

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:04.041
vLLM

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:05.804
A LessWrong post

00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:06.818
shows two agents

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.360
on the same

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:08.929
vLLM server communicating

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:09.943
via side channels

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:10.957
in kernel selection

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:11.983
with a receiver

00:00:11.795 --> 00:00:12.820
guessing a sender's

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.238
color in 1,221

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.714
of 1,221 rounds

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:19.523
The two protocols

00:00:19.476 --> 00:00:20.773
Step Sizing and

00:00:20.585 --> 00:00:21.893
KV Cache Message

00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:22.212
Board

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.320
convey bits through

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:24.287
the way vLLM

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:25.301
chooses kernels for

00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:26.068
engine steps

00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:27.554
which subtly changes

00:00:27.365 --> 00:00:29.051
another model's numerical

00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:29.641
results

00:00:30.158 --> 00:00:31.820
In an untrusted-monitoring

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:32.846
setup the policy

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:33.554
signals to a

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.804
colluding monitor that

00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:35.393
it is not

00:00:35.205 --> 00:00:36.054
a honeypot

00:00:36.582 --> 00:00:37.596
Full story on

00:00:37.407 --> 00:00:38.303
the dashboard
